-- title:
--   Chart line generic points are maximal in the special fibre
-- statement:
--   Let $O$ be a commutative ring, $\varpi \in O$, and $e$ a natural number, and assume that $O/(\varpi)$ is a domain. Write $\mathrm{chartScheme}\,\varpi = \operatorname{Spec}\bigl(O[X_0,X_1]/(X_0X_1 - \varpi)\bigr)$ for the crossing chart, and $\mathrm{Resolution}\,\varpi\,e$ for the colimit of the gluing diagram `glueDiagram` indexed by `GlueIndex e`, whose objects are copies of this chart; let $\mathrm{Resolution.toSpec}\,\varpi\,e$ be the composite of `toCrossing` with $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map $O \to O[X_0,X_1]/(X_0X_1-\varpi^e)$, a morphism $\mathrm{Resolution}\,\varpi\,e \to \operatorname{Spec} O$. Fix an index $k \in \mathrm{Fin}\,e$, with chart morphism `Resolution.ι ϖ e k` into the resolution, and a point $P$ of the chart whose prime ideal is the principal ideal generated by `U ϖ` or by `V ϖ` (by the cited computation, the two minimal primes over the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi$). Let $o$ be a point of $\mathrm{Resolution}\,\varpi\,e$ which specialises to `Resolution.ι ϖ e k P`, and which does not lie in the preimage under $\mathrm{Resolution.toSpec}\,\varpi\,e$ of the basic open set $D(\varpi) \subseteq \operatorname{Spec} O$. Then $o =$ `Resolution.ι ϖ e k P`.
--
--   This is the statement that the generic points of the two lines in each chart of the standard resolution of $uv = \varpi^e$ are maximal points of the special fibre, i.e. admit no strictly more generic point lying over $V(\varpi)$. It is the input needed for local analysis at the components of the special fibre, and is used in the construction of resolved Deligne–Rapoport style models of modular curves and in the attendant stalk and invertibility computations.
